164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (Eat Whole Foods: Focus on consuming whole, unprocessed foods like fruits, vegetables, lean proteins, and whole grains. These foods are more filling and nutrient-dense, helping you stay satisfied while reducing calorie intake. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (Stay Hydrated: Drink plenty of water throughout the day. Sometimes thirst can be mistaken for hunger, leading to unnecessary snacking. Aim for at least 8 glasses of water a day, and more if you're physically active. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (Prioritize Sleep: Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep per night. Poor sleep can disrupt hunger hormones, leading to increased appetite and cravings for unhealthy foods. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
